WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.635 --> 00:00:10.398
Then the jolly ghost vanished, and a cold, dark creature in a black hood came toward Scrooge.

2
00:00:11.419 --> 00:00:14.801
Unlike the other ghosts, this one was not friendly.

3
00:00:15.662 --> 00:00:17.783
In fact, he had the look of death.

4
00:00:17.803 --> 00:00:22.686
"You must be the Ghost of Christmas Future," inquired Scrooge.

5
00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:24.908
But the ghost said nothing.

6
00:00:27.724 --> 00:00:32.008
Pointing his bony finger, the ghost led Scrooge to a group of businessmen.

7
00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:35.370
"I heard he died last night," said one man.

8
00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.712
"I wonder who will get his money?"

9
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.354
joked another man.

10
00:00:39.374 --> 00:00:41.015
"He hasn't left it to me.

11
00:00:41.796 --> 00:00:45.279
That's all I know," said the first man, and he walked off.

12
00:00:45.299 --> 00:00:49.142
"Why are you showing me this?"

13
00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:50.423
asked Scrooge.

14
00:00:51.303 --> 00:00:53.545
But still the black ghost said nothing.

15
00:00:54.606 --> 00:00:56.448
Then they went to a group of servants.

16
00:00:57.376 --> 00:01:00.077
"Since he's dead, he doesn't need this.

17
00:01:00.597 --> 00:01:04.438
Quick, let's each take something," declared one maid.

18
00:01:04.458 --> 00:01:09.299
"He doesn't have any friends to claim his things," she continued.

19
00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:17.822
"We worked in his miserable house, so we earned it," said another.

20
00:01:18.842 --> 00:01:25.504
Scrooge watched in disgust as the servants divided silver spoons and other expensive things among themselves.

21
00:01:26.632 --> 00:01:29.894
Scrooge turned to the ghost saying, "I see!

22
00:01:30.654 --> 00:01:34.256
This could be me, if I do not change."

23
00:01:36.037 --> 00:01:39.559
The Ghost of Christmas Future took Scrooge to Bob Cratchit's house.

24
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.761
This time there was less joy there.

25
00:01:42.781 --> 00:01:45.802
"Did you visit Tiny Tim today, Father?"

26
00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:48.063
asked one of the children sadly.

27
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:52.806
"Yes, and I brought some flowers for his grave," he replied.

28
00:01:52.826 --> 00:01:56.228
"It is beautiful there," said Bob with a tear.

29
00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.763
For the first time ever, Scrooge felt true sorrow in his heart.

30
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:06.506
"Poor Bob," he thought.

31
00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.928
"He did love that boy."

32
00:02:09.568 --> 00:02:14.552
Then leaving that scene, Scrooge and the ghost traveled to a dreary graveyard.

33
00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:19.396
The spirit brought him to a grave where a coffin was being placed.

34
00:02:21.598 --> 00:02:23.760
There was no one there except a workman.

35
00:02:25.052 --> 00:02:31.696
Before Scrooge would look at the name on the new gravestone, he asked the ghost, "Spirit, tell me

36
00:02:31.756 --> 00:02:37.459
this, are these the things that will be or the things that might be?"

37
00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:40.180
The ghost made no response.

38
00:02:42.922 --> 00:02:49.205
Scrooge continued, "But if a man changes, then surely his future changes, right?

39
00:02:50.085 --> 00:02:52.087
If not, why would you visit me?"

40
00:02:52.867 --> 00:02:54.548
The ghost pointed to the grave.

41
00:02:55.656 --> 00:02:59.719
There on the gravestone was his name, Ebenezer Scrooge.

42
00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:04.223
With a loud cry, Scrooge declared, "This is not I.

43
00:03:04.243 --> 00:03:06.825
I am not this lonely man.

44
00:03:06.845 --> 00:03:17.033
No! I will honor Christmas in my heart, and try to keep it all the year.

45
00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:21.197
I will live in the past, the present, and the future.

46
00:03:22.057 --> 00:03:23.999
I will love others and help the poor.

47
00:03:24.619 --> 00:03:28.062
Please, give me another chance," pleaded Scrooge.

48
00:03:29.103 --> 00:03:32.865
At that, the dark ghost faded away in a puff of smoke.

49
00:03:35.787 --> 00:03:38.149
Scrooge found himself back in his bedroom.

50
00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:40.750
It was a bright, crisp morning.

51
00:03:41.691 --> 00:03:44.393
He was alive, and a completely new man.

52
00:03:45.473 --> 00:03:52.038
He opened his window and shouted to a boy walking along the street, "My good boy, what day

53
00:03:52.078 --> 00:03:52.798
is it today?"

54
00:03:52.818 --> 00:03:56.988
"Why, it is Christmas," replied the puzzled boy.

55
00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:02.310
shouted Scrooge.

56
00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.111
"I haven't missed it.

57
00:04:04.731 --> 00:04:09.492
My good boy, do you know the shop that has the very big turkey in its window?"

58
00:04:09.852 --> 00:04:10.572
asked Scrooge.

59
00:04:10.592 --> 00:04:13.233
"Of course," responded the boy.

60
00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.194
"An intelligent boy!

61
00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:18.835
Go and buy it, and bring it here," said Scrooge.

62
00:04:19.355 --> 00:04:23.076
"Come back in less than five minutes, and I'll give you half a crown!"

63
00:04:25.876 --> 00:04:27.517
The boy was off like a shot.

64
00:04:27.537 --> 00:04:29.838
"I'll send it to Bob Cratchit's!"

65
00:04:30.379 --> 00:04:31.219
laughed Scrooge.

66
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.141
"He won't know who sent it.

67
00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.562
It's twice the size of Tiny Tim."

68
00:04:37.282 --> 00:04:41.765
Then Scrooge dressed himself in his best clothes and went to visit his nephew.

69
00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:47.788
Before he could change his mind, he ran up and knocked on the door.

70
00:04:47.808 --> 00:04:49.329
"Uncle Scrooge?"

71
00:04:49.829 --> 00:04:51.710
said his nephew with great surprise.

72
00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:58.214
"If you are willing to have me, I'd like to dine with you tonight," said Scrooge.

73
00:05:00.756 --> 00:05:04.839
Scrooge's nephew almost shook his hand off because he was so pleased.

74
00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:09.142
Never did Scrooge have so much fun as he did that day.

75
00:05:10.083 --> 00:05:13.085
He ate and talked like he had never done before.

76
00:05:14.326 --> 00:05:17.508
After that Christmas Day, Scrooge became a different man.

77
00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.572
To Bob Cratchit, he became a wonderful employer.

78
00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:30.322
Bob's family suffered no more, and Scrooge provided money to help Tiny Tim, who did not die.

79
00:05:31.542 --> 00:05:34.783
In the city, he became known for his kindness and friendship.

80
00:05:35.783 --> 00:05:39.124
He put his money toward work to help the poor and suffering.

81
00:05:40.425 --> 00:05:42.165
He never saw the ghosts again.

82
00:05:43.146 --> 00:05:47.987
From that day on, it was always said of him that he knew how to keep Christmas well.

83
00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.088
May that be said of all of us!

84
00:05:52.029 --> 00:05:56.299
And as Tiny Tim said, "God bless everyone."
